# ---- line endings ----
# Store everything as LF inside the repository, but check out Windows-native CRLF for
# the files that actually need it.
#
# The .bat installers are the important case: cmd.exe is far less forgiving than
# PowerShell about a bare LF, and a broken install.bat is the first thing a new user
# would hit. *.ps1 gets CRLF too, purely because that is what Windows users expect to
# see when they open the file in an editor.
#
# *.md / *.json stay LF so the diffs stay readable on GitHub and the files behave the
# same on every platform.

* text=auto

*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
LICENSE    text eol=lf

# Binary safety net
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.zip  binary
*.exe  binary
